  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/kf0SkMhiqUsflQKHxUWOdfJ0uIoE_bh2Xq9554w046I.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\left(\\cot ^{-1} x\\right)^{2}-7\\left(\\cot ^{-1} x\\right)+10>0$\r\n\r\n$\\left(\\cot ^{-1} x-5\\right)\\left(\\cot ^{-1}-2\\right)>0$\r\n\r\n$\\cot ^{-1} x \\in(-\\infty, 2) \\cup(5, \\infty)$\r\n\r\nBut $\\cot ^{-1} x$ lies in $(0, \\pi)$\r\n\r\nNow, from equation (1)\r\n\r\n$\\cot ^{-1} x \\in(0,2)$\r\n\r\nNow, it is clear from the graph\r\n\r\n$x \\in(\\cot 2, \\infty)$",
    "image": null
